## Testing

- Frontend: no test framework yet — keep components pure and testable.
- Backend routers: test via `httpx.AsyncClient` with mocked `TaskManager` and `ResultReader`.
- New `routers/live.py`: mock `LivePortfolioState` reads, never touch real state files.
- WebSocket: test via FastAPI `TestClient.websocket_connect()`.

## What NOT to Do

- Never put business logic in React components — all computation in Python.
- Never use `any` in TypeScript — define proper interfaces in `types/index.ts`.
- Never use emoji for UI icons — use `lucide-react`.
- Never hardcode API URLs — use `BASE` constant from `api/client.ts`.
- Never use REST polling when WebSocket is available for task progress.
- Never use Recharts for financial price data — use `lightweight-charts`.
- Never add inline `<style>` tags — use Tailwind utilities.
